Project-specific draft prepared for legal review. This is not an official
PolyForm license and is not an OSI-approved open-source license. The terms
below are the proposed public terms offered with this snapshot; describing
them as a draft does not establish that a lawyer has reviewed them.

1. Licensor, scope, and prior rights

The offering licensor is Sina Mirshafiei, only for intellectual-property
rights that he owns or is authorized to offer. Other right holders retain
their rights. "Covered Material" means copyrightable original Peykar source,
documentation, configuration, and other material expressly offered under
this license. "You" means the person or organization exercising a right
that requires permission from the relevant right holder.

This license does not revoke, narrow, or replace a permission already
validly granted to a recipient under another license. An earlier private
Peykar 0.1.0 snapshot contained Apache-2.0 terms. If a recipient actually
obtained rights under that grant, those rights remain effective for the
material covered by that grant, subject to its conditions. Changing these
files does not withdraw that recipient's rights. This current distribution
does not make a new general Apache-2.0 offer for all its original code.
The historical text/checksums in licenses/ document that earlier snapshot
and existing rights; they are not a new grant to unlicensed material.
Separately licensed portions and existing rights must still be respected.

Third-party libraries, engines, models, datasets, and other separately
licensed material are excluded from Covered Material. Nothing here claims
ownership over their licenses or changes their permissions.

2. Allowed Noncommercial Purpose

An "Allowed Noncommercial Purpose" is personal study, noncommercial
experimentation, genuinely noncommercial teaching, public-benefit research,
or noncommercial community collaboration. The particular activity must
not have a Commercial Purpose defined in section 3. An organization's
nonprofit, academic, charitable, governmental, or open-source identity
does not by itself exempt an otherwise commercial activity.

Normal salaries, ordinary tuition supporting general teaching, donations,
and general research grants do not alone establish a Commercial Purpose.
They do not authorize a paid software service, a commissioned commercial
deliverable, or sponsor-directed commercial development. Donations must
not buy privileged access, a license, a service, or results. Grant or
sponsorship arrangements that require a commercial application or an
exclusive commercial deliverable are not an Allowed Noncommercial Purpose.

Humanitarian relief, disaster response, public-health research, environmental
protection, and other genuine public-benefit activities are expressly included
when the activity is noncommercial and recipients receive the software, access,
simulation service, and results without a required payment or other commercial
consideration. Recipients may use their own equipment or computing resources;
that alone is not charging for Peykar. General grants, unconditional donations,
and normal salaries may fund this work under the preceding paragraph. A donation
must be optional and must not affect eligibility, access, priority, or results.
Advertising-funded access, tied purchases, paid privileged tiers, and commercial
sponsor deliverables remain outside this public permission. Sharing must still
meet section 5, and external engines/data keep their separate terms.

3. Commercial Purpose and paid services

A "Commercial Purpose" includes an activity using Covered Material to:
(a) obtain revenue or other business advantage from software, access,
    subscriptions, advertising-supported access, API calls, or hosted use;
(b) sell, rent, commercially license, or otherwise charge for copies,
    modified versions, execution, or access to Covered Material;
(c) supply paid simulation, analysis, consulting, support, or other
    commissioned deliverables that substantially use Covered Material;
(d) conduct internal development, optimization, or research for a
    for-profit product, service, therapy, or other commercial offering;
(e) support a sponsor's commercial development, including where a
    university, charity, intermediary, or related entity performs the work;
(f) provide the same economic activity through an affiliate, a nominally
    free tier, a bundled price, a fee described as cost recovery, or an
    intermediary to avoid these conditions.

The absence of profit, a zero price for the software itself, publication
of source code, or nonprofit status alone does not make these activities
permitted. Paid uses listed here require a separate express grant from
the appropriate right holders. This public license provides no commercial
trial, automatic commercial entitlement, or future permissive conversion.

4. Conditional public permissions

For an Allowed Noncommercial Purpose, the relevant licensor permits You
to run, study, copy, modify, and share Covered Material, subject to every
condition below. No royalty is due for that permitted activity. Permission
to share applies to source and compiled forms and to noncommercial forks.

This permission is nonexclusive and worldwide for as long as You comply
with these conditions and the rights being licensed remain applicable.
Recipients obtain permissions directly from the relevant licensor under
the applicable terms; You may not represent that You can remove these
conditions from someone else's Covered Material.

5. Attribution, changes, and source access

When sharing Covered Material or a modified version, You must:
(a) include this license, NOTICE, and applicable third-party or historical
    notices; keep existing relevant authorship and attribution statements;
(b) identify Your changes and avoid presenting a modified version as an
    official release or a scientifically approved version;
(c) make the preferred form of the corresponding Covered Material and
    Your modifications available to recipients without a fee, together
    with the information reasonably needed to build that version;
(d) offer the modified Covered Material under these same noncommercial
    terms, without pretending to cancel separately applicable Apache or
    third-party permissions.

If You operate a modified version as a permitted noncommercial network
service, provide its users a visible, no-charge way to obtain that
corresponding source. These conditions do not require publication of
private noncommercial changes that You do not share or operate as such a
network service. They do not claim ownership of independent programs
merely because those programs communicate through an interface.

6. Data, findings, patents, and names

This license does not transfer ownership of a user's data, numerical
facts, scientific findings, or independently created works to the project.
It does not purport to copyright unprotected ideas or algorithms. Those
limits do not authorize otherwise restricted use of Covered Material.

Only to the extent the offering licensor has the power to do so, that
licensor grants the patent permission necessarily required to exercise
the permissions in section 4 for the Covered Material itself. No right
to patents on independent discoveries, biological products, treatments,
third-party technology, or a broader commercial application is implied.
No trademark, endorsement, or certification right is supplied by this text.

7. Separate agreements and contributions

The appropriate right holder may offer a separate written agreement.
Until such an agreement is signed by someone authorized to grant the
necessary rights, the restrictions of this public license still apply.
Silence, a download, an issue comment, or a contribution is not a commercial
authorization. These terms do not assign contributors' copyright to the
project owner or grant rights that a contributor has not actually supplied.

7A. Rights retained by the owner; separate commercial licensing

The conditions of this public grant restrict recipients relying on the grant.
They do not restrict Sina Mirshafiei's exercise of intellectual-property rights
that he himself owns or is otherwise independently authorized to exercise. For
those rights, he may use, modify, run, distribute, and commercially exploit his
own material, including in his own research, HomBon integration, products, and
services, without obtaining or paying for a public license from himself. He may
offer nonexclusive or exclusive commercial permissions by a separate written
agreement, within the rights he actually holds. An exclusive agreement cannot
cancel public permissions already validly granted to existing recipients.

This retained-rights statement is not an assignment of contributors' rights,
an exemption from a third party's license, or proof of ownership. A company or
other legal person, even one controlled by Sina Mirshafiei, is legally separate;
its rights must be established by applicable ownership rules or an express
written grant from the relevant right holders. A grant may be royalty-free.
No fee is imposed by this public license on the owner's exercise of his own
rights. Other contributors retain the same ability to exercise their own rights,
but cannot commercially license someone else's material without authorization.

8. Breach and termination

A material breach ends the permissions supplied by this license. Stop
activity that depends on those permissions. For a first inadvertent
failure solely to preserve attribution, notices, or the required source
access, permission may be restored if You fully correct the failure within
30 days after receiving written notice and take reasonable steps to
correct affected copies. That limited restoration does not authorize
commercial exploitation or extinguish a claim for an earlier breach.
Other restoration requires the relevant right holder's written agreement.

Any available remedy depends on applicable law and the actual rights,
conduct, and evidence. This text does not set automatic damages or guarantee
that a particular court will grant a remedy.

9. Risk and liability

Covered Material is supplied without promises of performance, scientific
accuracy, suitability for a particular task, noninfringement, maintenance,
or availability. To the extent applicable law permits, the offering
licensor does not accept liability for harm or loss arising from Covered
Material or its use. Mandatory liabilities that cannot legally be excluded
remain unaffected.

10. Mandatory rights, interpretation, and authority

This license does not remove statutory exceptions, mandatory consumer
rights, rights in the public domain, or permissions independently obtained
under another valid license. It does not prove copyright ownership or
copyrightability, including for AI-assisted material. Invalid or
unenforceable provisions do not enlarge the permissions beyond what the
remaining valid provisions actually grant.

The English text of this file is the operative project text. Translations,
README summaries, policy tables, and package identifiers are explanatory
and cannot contradict it or erase an earlier valid grant. No choice of
court, governing-law conclusion, or assurance of legal enforceability is
made merely by this draft. Qualified software/IP counsel should review
these terms, ownership, and the earlier Apache release before publication
or enforcement.
